        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The schedule is easy to remember: clean the pre-filter monthly, replace carbon every 3 to 6 months and HEPA every 6 to 12. What moves you within those ranges is how hard the purifier works. Smoke, pets, cooking, mold and nonstop running all push toward the short end, and a clean, dry bedroom can stretch toward the long one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Do not leave the decision to a timer. Use the light as a reminder to pull the filters and look, listen and smell. Replace what is spent, bag anything that has been catching mold, and budget for filters before you buy the purifier, because they are the real cost of keeping the air clean.
          </p>
